Internal Research End User Agreement for Academic and other Non-Profit Research
Institutions

Foundry Biosciences Inc. (hereafter "Foundry") is the owner of certain rights,
title and interest in the software and associated model weights, parameters,
and documentation made available in this repository (as further defined herein,
the "Software"), and has the right to grant licenses thereunder.

This Internal Research End User Agreement for Academic and other Non-Profit
Research Institutions (the "Agreement") sets forth the terms of use governing
your (the "End User") use of the Software. The Software is being released on
GitHub for free by Foundry to the End User solely for academic and/or internal
research purposes (the "Purpose").

FOR AVOIDANCE OF DOUBT, THE PURPOSE DOES NOT PERMIT: (1) USE OF THE SOFTWARE IN
HUMANS OR IN CONNECTION WITH HUMAN SUBJECTS, INCLUDING FOR DIAGNOSTIC OR OTHER
CLINICAL RESEARCH PURPOSES AND (2) USE OF THE SOFTWARE FOR COMMERCIAL RESEARCH
AND DEVELOPMENT PURPOSES.

Absent your agreement to the terms below, you (the "End User") have no right to
access or use the Software whatsoever.

Foundry agrees to grant, hereunder, a non-exclusive, non-transferable,
non-sublicensable license to End User for the use of the Software solely for
the Purpose on the following terms and conditions:

1. NO REDISTRIBUTION; RESTRICTIONS ON USE

Software remains the property of Foundry and End User shall not:

(a) publish, distribute, or otherwise transfer or make available the Software,
or any modification or derivative work of the Software (including any
fine-tuned, retrained or distilled model weights or parameters derived from the
Software), to any other third party for any purpose whatsoever, including by
hosting the Software or any outputs thereof as a service or making the Software
available through a public application programming interface or web interface;

(b) merge, reverse engineer, decompile or reverse assemble the Software or any
portion thereof;

Notwithstanding the foregoing, End User may modify, adapt, fine-tune, retrain
or otherwise create derivative works of the Software as reasonably necessary
for the Purpose, provided that any such modification or derivative work (i) is
used solely by End User for the Purpose, (ii) is subject to all of the terms
and conditions of this Agreement, including the restrictions set forth in
Section 1(a) and Section 2, and (iii) retains all notices as required by
Section 3. For the avoidance of doubt, nothing in this Section 1 limits End
User's right to publish results as provided in Section 4.

2. NO COMMERCIAL USE

End User shall use the Software for the Purpose only and shall not use the
Software for commercial purposes; any such use of the Software is expressly
prohibited. Commercial purposes include, but are not limited to, use of the
Software in fee-for-service arrangements, core facilities or laboratories, to
create or include within commercial products or services, or to provide
research services to third parties for a fee. If End User wishes to use
Software for commercial purposes, or for other purposes not permitted herein,
End User must execute a separate written license agreement with Foundry.

In order to request use of the Software for commercial purposes, or for other
purposes not permitted herein, please contact:

    Foundry Biosciences Inc.

    Email: licensing@foundrybio.ai

Notwithstanding the foregoing, and for avoidance of doubt, Foundry is under no
obligation to grant any commercial rights to an End User.

